-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Combs v. State\">403 So. 2d 418</a></span>; No. 81-5848, 277 S. C. 53, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9584082\"><a href=\"/opinion/1330854/state-v-gilbert/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Gilbert\">283 S. E. 2d 179</a></span>; No. 81-5944, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1662462\"><a href=\"/opinion/1662462/messer-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Messer v. State\">403 So. 2d 341</a></span>; No. 81-6385,<span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1378224\"><a href=\"/opinion/1378224/state-v-ortiz/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Ortiz\">131 Ariz. 195</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1378224\"><a href=\"/opinion/1378224/state-v-ortiz/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Ortiz\">639 P. 2d 1020</a></span>; No. 81-6435, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9722276\"><a href=\"/opinion/2125061/state-v-moore/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Moore\">210 Neb. 457</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9722276\"><a href=\"/opinion/2125061/state-v-moore/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Moore\">316 N. W. 2d 33</a></span>; No. 81-6437, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1106675\"><a href=\"/opinion/1106675/smith-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Smith v. State\">407 So. 2d 894</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9032401,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":594,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b1028-12\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"Ara\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"AOpj\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}